<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Uganda to withdraw troops from DR Congo town after army chief's threat sparks row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5eb38c08951f0c9be608a5821b25e1dbe3d979781eb8bf7c99e5b16162e3e697</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T17:56:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261127-uganda-withdraw-troops-dr-congo-town-after-army-chief-threat-row--7f3822a88887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261127-uganda-withdraw-troops-dr-congo-town-after-army-chief-threat-row" /><summary type="html">Uganda's army on Friday said it planned to withdraw from the eastern DR Congo town of Lubero in North Kivu. The announcement came days after Ugandan army chief Muhoozi Kainerugaba – son of President Yoweri Museveni – threatened to take control of Walikale, another North Kivu town, sparking a diplomatic spat between the two neighbouring nations.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Spain races to stop oil spill after ship capsizes off Ibiza</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7080e4797b6e5a0262973d36f60ac9a3361fc4fcddc34c937069da9b17235601</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T17:35:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-spain-races-to-stop-oil-spill-after-ship-capsizes-off-ibiza--a383d9b5a373.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-spain-races-to-stop-oil-spill-after-ship-capsizes-off-ibiza" /><summary type="html">Spanish authorities raced to contain any damage to ecologically valuable Mediterranean waters on Thursday after a tanker carrying up to 7,000 tonnes of diesel capsized off Ibiza, leaving one dead.</summary></entry><entry><title>French far-left candidate Mélenchon demands ‘thorough overhaul’ of Germany ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b90761c62799a198b797641c9c032f80dcf7ee736a8bda92d008378c7a40b0a0</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T17:31:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261127-french-far-left-candidate-m_lenchon-demands-thorough-overhaul-germany-ties--ddc9a03fffd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261127-french-far-left-candidate-m%C3%A9lenchon-demands-thorough-overhaul-germany-ties" /><summary type="html">Jean-Luc Mélenchon, leader of the hard-left France Unbowed (LFI) party, on Friday declared he was "hostile" to German economic liberalism and its dominance of the European Union. The septuagenarian presidential candidate in the 2027 race also warned that France could be drawn into unwanted conflict as Germany's growing military strength makes it a "target" for other countries.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>OM - Levski Sofia: A night of violence disrupts Marseille match</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89e457d4f71bd14031e40f7bfc18bf3a48a2b7e1e25a5de3e9b93a7a21beb0a0</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T17:29:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-om-levski-sofia-a-night-of-violence-disrupts-marseille-match--ef6bcf6a1a34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-om-levski-sofia-a-night-of-violence-disrupts-marseille-match" /><summary type="html">🇫🇷 ⚽ 🇧🇬 At least 11 supporters of Bulgarian football club #LevskiSofia were injured in Marseille on Thursday, as skirmishes broke out between the visiting club and fans of hosts Olympique Marseille (#OM) before their Europa League fixture,
 
FRANCE 24 has the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paris Paloma tackles Greek mythology, generative AI in her second album 'The Fatal Flaw'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6e3f81b1c8c24986b48f3eca6371a9e29e19c5e0d40997303e42dcf2dd02d97</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T17:25:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261127-paris-paloma-tackles-greek-mythology-generative-ai-in-her-second-album-the-fatal-flaw--45c48c39b045.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261127-paris-paloma-tackles-greek-mythology-generative-ai-in-her-second-album-the-fatal-flaw" /><summary type="html">Dheepthika Laurent chats with Paris Paloma on set ahead of her Paris concert. The UK singer-songwriter and guitarist is promoting her second album, "The Fatal Flaw", an ode to Greek mythology, art and feminism. She tells us why this album is more personal than her first record, "Cacophony".</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>France is dealing with water insecurity – a new study shows it's a global problem</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04618ddc2b42233ce08fe36d02c4fde083919b0a84e2fca9b10e46f6db2b1f9e</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T17:10:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/environment/20261127-france-dealing-with-water-insecurity-_-new-study-shows-global-problem--9c96eec6f76c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261127-france-dealing-with-water-insecurity-%E2%80%93-new-study-shows-global-problem" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of people in France are living under water restrictions as the country deals with a drought despite recent rains, according to the environment ministry. But this is a global problem, as a new study released Wednesday revealed "the largest global decline in surface water resources recorded" since 1991, when data collection began.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Big EU defence projects under threat from proposed budget cuts: Commissioner Andrius Kubilius</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2c9818413361ae0461c8948cb5d52bfcfe8b2448962a0a712483852bd629771</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T17:03:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261127-big-eu-defence-projects-under-threat-from-proposed-budget-cuts-commissioner-andrius-kubiliu--50d516346b36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261127-big-eu-defence-projects-under-threat-from-proposed-budget-cuts-commissioner-andrius-kubilius" /><summary type="html">We speak to the EU's Commissioner for Defence and Space, Andrius Kubilius. The former prime minister of Lithuania – who grew up during the Soviet era – tells us how he sees the confrontation between Europe and Russia. He also sounds the alarm over proposed cuts in the EU's future budget, saying that they could jeopardise major European projects in defence and space. Kubilius praises the EU's SAFE defence loans programme, remarking that it has been "really very successful".</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>From cyberbullying to extremist content, can EU Kids Act protect minors online?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f6313912bace7bc0c494e98c4c0a33e071547dd37e1931bbea8a0ce3660449e</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T17:02:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261127-from-cyberbullying-to-extremist-content-can-eu-kids-act-protect-minors-online--b1948edc7546.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261127-from-cyberbullying-to-extremist-content-can-eu-kids-act-protect-minors-online" /><summary type="html">Almost every European teenager is online. Some 96 percent of 15-year-olds use social media, yet many say they do not feel safe there. One in four children in the EU, aged 12 to 17, report having experienced cyberbullying, and nearly one in three say social media has left them feeling stressed, sad or socially excluded.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Asia and Europe stocks rally after volatile week</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b458971328126affb17d0325c0636ede78d93be2139c09a61143892e25bbb278</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:43:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-asia-and-europe-stocks-rally-after-volatile-week--50bb9ab0d4e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-asia-and-europe-stocks-rally-after-volatile-week" /><summary type="html">Stocks jumped on Wall Street on Friday, putting markets on track for strong weekly gains despite several days of erratic swings. Jameel Ahmad, Chief Analyst at GTC, tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Turkey summons Georgian envoy after football fans' pro-Palestine protest sparks clashes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b4c1bf6294150a44178036c3e0d0647bdc69b01d7aefa2c191b3a5e6e937733</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:37:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261127-turkey-summons-georgian-envoy-after-football-fans-pro-palestine-protest-sparks-clashes--4d4c8ca9f298.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261127-turkey-summons-georgian-envoy-after-football-fans-pro-palestine-protest-sparks-clashes" /><summary type="html">Turkey summoned ​Georgia's ambassador on ​Friday over violence that broke out ​at ‌a Europa ⁠League match in Batumi ‌between the Turkish Besiktas ⁠and Israeli Hapoel Beer-Sheva teams, according to a foreign ministry source. Clashes erupted after Besiktas fans unfurled a pro-Palestinian banner during the match, sparking the diplomatic row.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Sierra Leone: Maternal deaths fall as healthcare improves, but challenges remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2a0545028dda6c3a42388b2d736b570379c2b5a2671794fa0116137407f68f2</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:37:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-sierra-leone-maternal-deaths-fall-as-healthcare-improves-but-challenges-remain--31f3611f9d60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-sierra-leone-maternal-deaths-fall-as-healthcare-improves-but-challenges-remain" /><summary type="html">Sierra Leone was once considered one of the most dangerous countries in the world to give birth. Maternal deaths have since fallen dramatically, thanks to improvements in healthcare, medical training and maternity services. But despite this progress, significant challenges remain. Activists warn that continued efforts are needed to ensure safer pregnancies and childbirth for women across the country. Clarisse Fortuné reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Macron lashes out at Le Pen’s ‘arrogance’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c916a06a54d1f45dd3af0b2b8937b0155120d7daf0d104b62232bcb315a24e53</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:35:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-france-macron-lashes-out-at-le-pen-s-arrogance--b86653cd7fbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-france-macron-lashes-out-at-le-pen-s-arrogance" /><summary type="html">🇫🇷 French President Emmanuel #Macron on Thursday responded to far-right leader and 2027 presidential candidate Marine #LePen’s claim that he was “blocking” the French people’s freedom of expression.
 
Listen in to what he had to say.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo: Copper reserves put Africa at the centre of the global race for critical minerals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e56aed81a832ea33d38fc5db8b4c026e0726fa5eae069664006c81106ad96e2</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:30:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-dr-congo-copper-reserves-put-africa-at-the-centre-of-the-global-race-for-critical-minerals--aa0f8367804e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-dr-congo-copper-reserves-put-africa-at-the-centre-of-the-global-race-for-critical-minerals" /><summary type="html">Africa is emerging as a key player in the global race for copper, accounting for around 10 per cent of the world's estimated reserves. The Democratic Republic of Congo is at the centre of this growing interest, having mined 3.4 million metric tons of copper in 2025. Its vast mineral resources are attracting growing attention from countries and companies around the world, as demand for the metal rises due to its importance in energy infrastructure, electric vehicles and the global transition to cleaner energy.</summary></entry><entry><title>With Spain’s far right on the cusp of power, can women bail Sanchez out once again?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1266dcb90973d3b86876940ab224cac2dbe8546e45bffabb57f2372b79686011</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:27:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261127-spain-far-right-vox-at-the-gates-can-women-bail-out-sanchez-once-again--5cb7f43b4608.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261127-spain-far-right-vox-at-the-gates-can-women-bail-out-sanchez-once-again" /><summary type="html">Spanish women’s refusal to surrender hard-won rights helped Socialist Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez clinch an unlikely victory in a snap election three years ago. As he gambles with another early vote on Sunday, his hopes of defying the odds rest on women again rallying to block the far right from governing Spain for the first time since Francisco Franco’s dictatorship.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: Political violence and attacks on candidates raise fears ahead of January elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae10a418856aba3513048b41752cbc5ffab1ae6ea104bd8713942bc618bde755</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:25:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-nigeria-political-violence-and-attacks-on-candidates-raise-fears-ahead-of-january-elections--38f96b50082e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-nigeria-political-violence-and-attacks-on-candidates-raise-fears-ahead-of-january-elections" /><summary type="html">Political violence is escalating in Nigeria ahead of the general elections scheduled for January. Candidates and their supporters have increasingly come under attack, with armed groups disrupting campaign rallies and some assaults resulting in deaths. Despite the growing number of incidents, security forces have struggled to contain the violence. With less than two months to go before the vote, fears are mounting that intimidation and deadly attacks could prevent many Nigerians from freely taking part in the democratic process.</summary></entry><entry><title>French student protests: A 'very bizarre' government response</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78bd7eb21df2ca9aa929b962263ba1015cadc82e043950e369be2e4746d5a628</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:04:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-student-movement-in-france-the-situation-has-varied-greatly-from-one-school-to-another--3b4143268c97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-student-movement-in-france-the-situation-has-varied-greatly-from-one-school-to-another" /><summary type="html">“The government had a very bizarre way of dealing with the student protests,” says Jean-Rémi Girard, a secondary school teacher and union representative in Asnières-sur-Seine. He explains how teachers sought to defuse tensions by listening to students, and respecting their right to protest, while keeping classes running. He recounts a police intervention last October and the case of a student facing trial for defending a classmate, and has the full support of several teachers. Girard questions the government's heavy-handed policing and largely symbolic proposals on class sizes and university admissions. “There wasn't really a negotiation,” he says, also highlighting the number of education workers injured during the protests.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bulgarian fans injured after clashes between supporters at Marseille-Levski game in Europa League</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4264473e7d378e52e836d493470ac926f31be41c5ebc124331603c2bbf0e8d0c</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T15:58:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-bulgarian-fans-injured-after-clashes-between-supporters-at-marseille-levski-game-in-europa---8d2bba183856.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-bulgarian-fans-injured-after-clashes-between-supporters-at-marseille-levski-game-in-europa-league" /><summary type="html">French and Bulgarian authorities condemned the violence that left at least 11 Bulgarian soccer fans injured during clashes between Marseille and Levski Sofia supporters before their Europa League match on Thursday evening, and Marseille prosecutors opened two investigations.</summary></entry><entry><title>Back to Black Friday: 'We are now bombarded with offers throughout the year'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:064ef744e4fd9404a2623a605e614e954f3cc0d4814208fa2ef2ee701761715f</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T15:53:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-black-friday-how-the-global-shopping-phenomenon-is-evolving-amid-the-cost-of-living-crisis--7abf501085a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-black-friday-how-the-global-shopping-phenomenon-is-evolving-amid-the-cost-of-living-crisis" /><summary type="html">Black Friday was once a single day of holiday sales, held the day after Thanksgiving. Then retailers began kicking things off a day early, on Thanksgiving itself. “We are now bombarded with offers throughout the year,” says Hilary Ingham, Professor of Economics and Department Head at Lancaster University, who has no plans to shop this Black Friday. Ingham acknowledges a growing sense of “retail fatigue” but still sees the potential for a peak in sales. Meanwhile, an investigation by The Telegraph suggests that six in ten of the most popular products were actually more expensive than earlier in the year, underscoring the need for consumers to remain vigilant and track prices over time.</summary></entry><entry><title>Under a new flag, North Korea carves out identity as fully fledged nuclear state</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3c7acade769676df65ea7d0c2c3d73b8d5fbdd9541def3dadfa25260083eba9</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T15:51:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261127-under-a-new-flag-north-korea-carves-out-identity-as-fully-fledged-nuclear-state--8c1426726518.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261127-under-a-new-flag-north-korea-carves-out-identity-as-fully-fledged-nuclear-state" /><summary type="html">North Korea has modified its national flag as part of a constitutional amendment. The text also enshrined the country's status as a nuclear power and removed any reference to the "peaceful reunification" pursued by Kim Jong Un's predecessors. Meanwhile, the reclusive leader has been keen to demonstrate his desire to expand diplomatic ties with friendly nations. Yuka Royer speaks with Edward Howell of Oxford University to put these recent developments into context.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>France: David Lisnard shakes up presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab04d5ff75f866c6bb0eaffcaa3d5c89f67454a55775d64f762d42a0f3700c72</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T15:51:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-france-david-lisnard-shakes-up-presidential-race--632f3b4b1d6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-france-david-lisnard-shakes-up-presidential-race" /><summary type="html">David Lisnard, the mayor of Cannes and a candidate in France's 2027 presidential election, has climbed to third place in several opinion polls. His rise is shaking up the political landscape on the right and centre. We discuss what this means with France 24's James André.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: How much have Europeans spent on aid?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:819c0d747c1919c22351348b64471284ddc25dea5153e7957a5feb6772be6686</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T15:41:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-ukraine-how-much-have-europeans-spent-on-aid--dbe02003986a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-ukraine-how-much-have-europeans-spent-on-aid" /><summary type="html">Since Russia's full-scale invasion in 2022, EU member states have provided around €200 billion in aid to Ukraine, making them its largest contributors ahead of the United States. Germany leads in total financial contributions, with around €54 billion, roughly twice France's €27 billion. But the picture changes when aid is measured against GDP or per capita, with Denmark and other Nordic countries ranking among the biggest contributors.</summary></entry><entry><title>With new law, Iraq sees rise in child marriage, custody battles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6b512b1ebd720a653fc21f654dd7bca1ad1aa57a767ff9a43396010ac28d7f0</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:48:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261127-with-new-law-iraq-sees-rise-in-child-marriage-custody-battles--d28ba6fc52bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261127-with-new-law-iraq-sees-rise-in-child-marriage-custody-battles" /><summary type="html">In January 2025, Iraq's parliament passed an amendment allowing families to place their household under religious law, governing all issues around marriage, divorce and inheritance. The new Ja'fari law, a Shiite law, came into force in October 2025. One year on, its consequences have been raising serious alarm, especially among women, who say they've seen a major rollback of their rights. FRANCE 24's Marie-Charlotte Roupie reports, with Josh Vardey.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Japan's radical past: Retracing the far-left groups of the 1970s</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcf33bda5cd003bd87c1d08760fcd73c1f06402fe9c31debf6478a5dd55f7d6c</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:33:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261127-japan-radical-past-retracing-far-left-groups-1970s--9e5d65caa965.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261127-japan-radical-past-retracing-far-left-groups-1970s" /><summary type="html">Our correspondents delve into the history of Japan's radical left in the 1970s. From the United Red Army to the Japanese Red Army, several movements turned to armed struggle and violent action. More than half a century on, our team met with two former militants.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>US: Thanksgiving storms cause flooding and travel chaos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0db8e704b898c506cddbc2ca19331084de24a267fd6c93fddb1729e24cda511c</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:02:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-us-thanksgiving-storms-cause-flooding-and-travel-chaos--00eaeda87816.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-us-thanksgiving-storms-cause-flooding-and-travel-chaos" /><summary type="html">Severe storms battered the US East Coast on Thursday, bringing torrential rain, strong winds and coastal flooding. Nearly one million homes were left without power, while hundreds of flights were cancelled and thousands delayed during one of the country's busiest travel periods. The weather also forced the postponement of New York's Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade until Saturday.</summary></entry></feed>
